Charles000@aol.com said :

> Have you had a look at Romana Machado's excellent encrypting
> technique (as per her Stego software) for embedding numerical
> data into the pixel data sets of a bit map image???  Maybe this is
> a bit far fetched, but I like her ideas about being able to "mask"
> hidden information "inside" a bit map file, to the extent that this
> could be a stealth signature embedded directly into the image.

Of course, if you strip out the LSB of each pixel of any pirated
images, then it will remove any hidden signature. Equally, changing to
a lossy compression format, gamma-correcting true color images,
scaling, cropping, etc, will destroy any encrypted signature unless it
uses heavy-duty error correction.

In other words, you can create a signature algorithm which will prevent
people from copying images if they don't know how your signature is
hidden, but as soon as a signature algorithm becomes popular, tools will
appear to defeat it. Just as with software copy protection, it will
only prevent casual copying.

		Mark

